# Claude Code — environment variables
# Setup: copy this file to .claude/.env and fill in the values. Never commit .claude/.env
#
# Resolution order (highest to lowest):
#   1. process.env                        runtime
#   2. .claude/skills/<skill>/.env         per-skill override
#   3. .claude/skills/.env                 shared by all skills
#   4. .claude/.env                        project-wide default (this file)
#
# Debug: python3 .claude/scripts/resolve_env.py --show-hierarchy

# ============================================
# Google Gemini — skill: ai-multimodal
# ============================================
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional — rotate across several keys when rate limited
# (see .claude/skills/common/api_key_rotator.py)
# GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_3=

# Optional — model overrides
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# GEMINI_IMAGE_GEN_MODEL=

# Optional — use Vertex AI instead of AI Studio
# GEMINI_USE_VERTEX=true
# VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=
# VERTEX_LOCATION=us-central1

# ============================================
# Context7 — skill: docs-seeker, and the context7 MCP server
# ============================================
# Get a key at https://context7.com/dashboard/api-keys
# CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# ============================================
# MCP servers
# ============================================
# MCP servers are configured in .mcp.json (project scope), not through this file.
# Start from the template:  cp .claude/.mcp.json.example .mcp.json
#
# The template covers the servers these skills need:
#   pencil               required by ui-design-pencil (71 references)
#   sequential-thinking  backs the sequential-thinking skill
#   context7             docs lookup; paste CONTEXT7_API_KEY into its --api-key arg
#
# Note: the pencil entry points at a local macOS arm64 app binary
# (/Applications/Pen.app/...). On another machine or architecture, get the correct
# path from that machine's Pencil install before using it.
#
# Servers can also be registered globally in ~/.claude.json instead of per project.
